{"duration": 57.573, "exact_word_timing": true, "lines": [{"beat": 0, "text": "A U.S. engineer surveyed a swamp, notebook in hand.", "start": 0.08, "end": 3.25}, {"beat": 1, "text": "Workers complained of endless fevers and aching bodies.", "start": 3.67, "end": 6.512}, {"beat": 2, "text": "Yellow fever and malaria killed thousands during construction.", "start": 6.932, "end": 10.262}, {"beat": 3, "text": "You see, it\u2019s like ignoring a leak until the whole house floods.", "start": 10.682, "end": 13.787}, {"beat": 4, "text": "Colonel William Gorgas organized a massive sanitation drive.", "start": 14.207, "end": 17.636}, {"beat": 4, "text": "He divided the zone into districts and sent inspectors to find mosquito larvae.", "start": 17.856, "end": 22.424}, {"beat": 4, "text": "Carpenters removed standing water, and crews spread oil on any remaining pools.", "start": 22.644, "end": 26.924}, {"beat": 4, "text": "Screens were installed on windows and over sleeping areas.", "start": 27.144, "end": 30.067}, {"beat": 4, "text": "Every worker received free medical care and yearly quinine for malaria.", "start": 30.287, "end": 34.205}, {"beat": 4, "text": "Gorgas also fumigated homes with sulfur and pyrethrum, using the entire U.S. supply.", "start": 34.425, "end": 40.162}, {"beat": 4, "text": "He set up quarantine cages for anyone showing fever.", "start": 40.382, "end": 43.325}, {"beat": 5, "text": "By 1906 yellow\u2011fever cases fell to one, then none at all.", "start": 43.745, "end": 47.618}, {"beat": 5, "text": "Malaria deaths dropped sharply, saving thousands of lives.", "start": 47.838, "end": 51.022}, {"beat": 6, "text": "The canal opened not just because of engineers,", "start": 51.442, "end": 53.944}, {"beat": 6, "text": "but because mosquitoes were finally defeated.", "start": 54.164, "end": 56.453}], "words": [{"w": "A", "start": 0.149, "end": 0.199, "line": 0, "beat": 0}, {"w": "U.S.", "start": 0.274, "end": 0.974, "line": 0, "beat": 0}, {"w": "engineer", "st